  "Description": "Converts a float value into a string.\n\nThe Format input accepts a .NET composite format string. Examples for the value 1.2345:\n\n{0:P1} -> 123.5 %\n{0:000.000} -> 001.235\n{0:0} -> 1\n{0:G3} -> 1.23\nneed {0:0.0} cookies -> need 1.2 cookies\n\nSee also: [IntToString], [Vec3ToString]",
